\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Phenological distributions and variance partitioning of intra-urban and inter-urban components}. Panels (a) and (d) show the proportional contributions of intra-urban (dark gray) and inter-urban (light gray) components to variation in SOS and EOS, respectively, as estimated from mixed-effects models. Each bar associated with the phylogenetic tree represents one species. Panels (b) and (e) illustrate city-level distributions of the SOS (b) and EOS (e) for four representative species which differ in the proportion of variance. The colored horizontal bars indicate the median (dots) and the interquartile range (IQR, bar ends) within each city. The shaded areas represent the median and IQR of city-level median phenological dates. Panels (c) and (f) compare intra-urban (y-axis) and inter-urban (x-axis) IQR for all species, for SOS and EOS respectively. The dashed 1:1 line indicates where intra- and inter-urban variability would be equal.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig2:variance}{{2}{11}{}{figure.2}{}}
